  "n1": {
   "x": 2350,
   "y": 300,
   "w": 340,
   "fill": "purple",
   "text": "Design tokens used (from your app)\nMontserrat. brandPrimary #6D1A95, brandDeep #3B0764, tint #F3E8FF, scaffold #F9F7FA, text #1E1B4B, muted #6B7280.\nRadii: card 22, input and button 16, chip 12.\nPending status is purple on lavender, never amber. Placeholders are in [brackets]."
  },
  "n2": {
   "x": 2350,
   "y": 860,
   "w": 340,
   "fill": "orange",
   "text": "Entry, tabs, events, tours, academy and profile: redrawn from the IDE spec\nBoards tagged MATCH TO YOUR APP exist in your app. I drew them from the spec and my own assumptions, so compare with your real screens and tell me what differs.\nBoards tagged NEW are screens your app does not have yet."
  },
  "n3": {
   "x": 2350,
   "y": 1420,
   "w": 340,
   "fill": "red",
   "text": "Flags before building\n1. A bank slip or SWIFT copy can be forged. Treat it as a claim and release the next step only after bank confirmation.\n2. The ECTA price floor needs a real, sourced data feed before the bid builder enforces it.\n3. Show Verified Regulatory Data on AI answers only when they cite a stored source.\n4. The public verify page says what was checked and never says compliant."
  },
  "n4": {
   "x": 2350,
   "y": 2060,
   "w": 340,
   "fill": "green",
   "text": "Still not drawn\nContract e-sign S-121, inspection and shipping S-123/124, settlement S-125, dispute room S-126, suspended state S-130, unified checkout S-132, document vault S-133, team seats S-107, verification status timeline S-109."
